      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the structure. The original test has significant understandability issues:\n- Dead code: several unused helper methods and the broken `private T __super_createEmptyFilter(Shape shape)` abstract-looking declaration\n- Methods using undefined generic type `T` (`createFilter` returning `T`) that are never called by `testClear`\n- The actual test logic is only 4 lines but buried under ~100 lines of irrelevant scaffolding\n\nI'll write a clean version with only what's needed for `testClear`.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored `SparseBloomFilterTest_testClear.java` removes all unused helper methods and dead code (including the broken generic `T` declarations), keeping only the three focused helpers (`getTestShape`, `createEmptyFilter`, `createFilter`) that `testClear` actually needs, with brief comments explaining the test intent."
